  "id": "action-identification",
  "term": "action identification",
  "definition": "Action identification is the process of deciding what action another person is performing from what is observed. In the source context, it refers to judging whether an actor is engaging with or withdrawing from an object, and this judgment can be shaped by prior experience and explicit expectations about that person’s usual behaviour.",
